    "body": "LOGICAL_AGENT = LESTER\nROLE = TECH / REPAIR\nASSIGNED_BY = JINGO\nOWNER = SPARX\nSTATE = ASSIGNED / REPAIR REQUIRED\n\n## AUTHORITY\nParent implementation: issue #47\nIndependent QC: issue #48\nRejected exact HEAD: `7285aa76ee678b3059ec4db22b5b4fb193b131df`\nDUNCAN verdict comment: `5427879712`\n\nTASK 7 remains BLOCKED.\nNo production model download/configuration.\nNo live SALVADOR generation.\nNo merge.\n\n## REPAIR SCOPE — EXACTLY FIVE IMPORTANT FINDINGS\n\n### 1. FAILED must be terminal in orchestration\nCurrent repro: durable FAILED can fall through and submit again.\nRequired behavior:\n- durable FAILED suppresses backend submission;\n- local/result checks must not override terminal FAILED semantics;\n- add regression test proving repeated discovery after FAILED causes zero new submit calls.\n\n### 2. Single-SALVADOR GPU lock must survive controller restart\nCurrent repro: after restart, ASSIGNED can be encountered before durable RUNNING and submit before active state is reconstructed.\nRequired behavior:\n- reconstruct all durable active RUNNING executions before dispatching any new ASSIGNED task in a cycle;\n- at most one SALVADOR GPU task may be active across restart/reorder;\n- add regression with issue order [ASSIGNED, RUNNING] proving zero new submit.\n\n### 3. Reconcile GitHub durable-event publication failures\nTwo required recovery paths:\nA. result persisted but RESULT_READY comment failed -> next cycle must heal/post missing RESULT_READY without regenerating.\nB. backend accepted prompt_id but RUNNING comment failed -> controller must retain/reconstruct execution identity and must NOT resubmit same task after restart; next cycle must reconcile durable RUNNING or otherwise track the accepted execution safely.\n\nRequired tests must inject post failures and prove:\n- no duplicate backend submission;\n- missing durable state is eventually repaired;\n- valid local result never causes a second generation merely because RESULT_READY publication previously failed.\n\n### 4. Malformed TASK_ID must not crash polling cycle\nCurrent repro: `TASK_ID = ..\\\\outside` reaches path layer and `PathBoundaryError` escapes `run_once`.\nRequired behavior:\n- validate TASK_ID against explicit path-safe grammar in task contract OR convert path-boundary failure into per-task deterministic failure;\n- malformed marked issue is isolated; controller continues processing other issues in same/later cycle;\n- no arbitrary path accepted;\n- add regression proving polling process survives malformed TASK_ID.\n\n### 5. Add execution deadline / timeout\nCurrent behavior: backend can report RUNNING forever.\nRequired behavior:\n- configured maximum execution duration owned by deployment config, not issue text;\n- once deadline exceeded, task transitions durably to FAILED with stable error code (e.g. `EXECUTION_TIMEOUT`);\n- timeout must not submit a replacement execution automatically;\n- tests use injected/fake clock, not real sleeps.\n\n## PRESERVE CONFIRMED PASSING BOUNDARIES\nDo not regress:\n- strict AGENT/TASK_KIND/STATE/REFERENCE allowlists;\n- fixed-root local filesystem boundary + traversal rejection;\n- image extension/magic/size validation;\n- fixed argv `gh` + `shell=False`;\n- missing/unauthed gh safe configuration failure;\n- metadata-only durable events;\n- non-empty prompt_id required before RUNNING;\n- persistence before RESULT_READY publication attempt;\n- zero paid API / zero OPENAI_API_KEY;\n- no production-model dependency for mocked phase;\n- no runtime repo writes / merge / OWNER LOCK / runtime activation authority.\n\n## IMPLEMENTATION LAW\nUse TDD / regression-first for each finding:\n1. Add failing negative regression reproducing Duncan finding.\n2. Run it and capture RED.\n3. Implement minimal fix.\n4. Run targeted test GREEN.\n5. Run full suite.\n\nDo not broaden scope or refactor unrelated code.\n\n## REQUIRED HANDOFF\nWhen repair begins:\n`LESTER_LOCAL_CONTROLLER_REPAIR_RUNNING`\n\nWhen ready for re-QC:\n```text\nLESTER_LOCAL_CONTROLLER_REPAIR_COMPLETE\nBASE_REJECTED_HEAD = 7285aa76ee678b3059ec4db22b5b4fb193b131df\nREPAIR_HEAD = <exact sha>\nFINDING_1_FAILED_TERMINAL = FIXED / TEST=<name>\nFINDING_2_RESTART_GPU_LOCK = FIXED / TEST=<name>\nFINDING_3_EVENT_RECONCILIATION = FIXED / TEST=<names>\nFINDING_4_TASK_ID_ISOLATION = FIXED / TEST=<name>\nFINDING_5_EXECUTION_TIMEOUT = FIXED / TEST=<name>\nFULL_TESTS = <fresh exact output>\nCOMPILE = <fresh exact output>\nPRODUCTION_MODEL = NOT TOUCHED\nLIVE_COMFYUI = NOT CALLED\nTASK_7 = REQUEST_DUNCAN_RE_QC\nMERGE = NO\n```\n\nDUNCAN must independently re-QC the new exact REPAIR_HEAD. Task 7 remains blocked until DUNCAN PASS.",
